-- title:
--   Logarithm of a narrow ray class L-series as a prime sum
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field, let $\mathfrak f$ be a non-zero ideal of $\mathcal O_K$, and let $\chi$ be a monoid homomorphism from `NarrowRayClassGroup K 𝔣` into the multiplicative monoid of $\mathbb C$ (no unitarity or finite-order condition is imposed); here the group in question is the quotient of the subgroup `coprimeToModulus K 𝔣` of invertible fractional ideals $I$ of $K$ whose $v$-adic count `FractionalIdeal.count K v I` vanishes at every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_K$ dividing $\mathfrak f$, by the intersection with it of `narrowRaySubgroup K 𝔣`, the subgroup generated by `narrowRaySet K 𝔣`. The assertion is that there exists $\Lambda : \mathbb R \to \mathbb C$ which is continuous on the open half-line $(1,\infty)$, satisfies $\exp(\Lambda(s)) = \sum_{C} \chi(C)\,\mathrm{rayZeta}_K(\mathfrak f, C; s)$ for every real $s > 1$ (the sum over all narrow ray classes $C$ of $\chi(C)$ times the $L$-series of the coefficient function `rayZetaCoeff`, evaluated at $s$ viewed in $\mathbb C$), such that for every real $s > 1$ the family $v \mapsto \chi_{\mathrm{ideal}}(v)\,N(v)^{-s}$, indexed by the height-one spectrum of $\mathcal O_K$, is summable, and such that for some constant $C \in \mathbb R$ independent of $s$ one has $\bigl\|\Lambda(s) - \sum_{v} \chi_{\mathrm{ideal}}(v)\,N(v)^{-s}\bigr\| \le C$ for all real $s > 1$. Here $N$ is `Ideal.absNorm`, the exponent is $-(s:\mathbb C)$, and $\chi_{\mathrm{ideal}}(v) =$ `chiIdeal K 𝔣 χ` of the fractional ideal attached to $v$, namely the value of $\chi$ on the class of that ideal when it is non-zero and lies in `coprimeToModulus K 𝔣`, and $0$ otherwise.
--
--   This is the logarithmic form of the Euler product for a Hecke $L$-series attached to a character of a narrow ray class group: $\log L(s,\chi)$ agrees with the prime sum $\sum_{\mathfrak p} \chi(\mathfrak p) N\mathfrak p^{-s}$ up to a bounded error on $s>1$, with a continuous branch of the logarithm provided. It is used in the analytic estimates for prime sums over height-one primes in cyclotomic extensions, [`NumberField.exists_forall_abs_tsum_absNorm_rpow_neg_sub_inv_finrank_mul_log_le_of_isCyclotomicExtension`](thm.html#NumberField.exists_forall_abs_tsum_absNorm_rpow_neg_sub_inv_finrank_mul_log_le_of_isCyclotomicExtension) and [`NumberField.exists_forall_le_tsum_absNorm_rpow_neg_of_isCyclotomicExtension`](thm.html#NumberField.exists_forall_le_tsum_absNorm_rpow_neg_of_isCyclotomicExtension).
